{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>See, I</b> — singular language. Interpreted: \"See\" is said to each and every one. Others say: to Joshua He said, \"See, I,\" and warned him to bless Israel when they cross the Jordan. Others say: because the curses and blessings in Mishneh Torah were all said in singular language. Another interpretation: \"See, I\" — see the Ten Commandments, which open with \"I,\" and fulfill them, for all the commandments are included in them. Another interpretation: \"See, I\" — from Me you shall see, and thus you shall do. Another interpretation: \"See\" — singular; \"before you\" — plural. And that is what we say: How was the order of the Mishnah? Moses reviewed to Aaron his chapter, and afterward his sons entered, etc., as in Eruvin. Another interpretation: Above it is written \"to you,\" and adjacent to it: \"See, I give before you today blessing\" — meaning, to you I say, that you choose the blessing. Another interpretation: \"See\" — one who casts a lot with his fellow covers the lots and the portions so that his fellow not choose the good portion, but you — see the lots and see the portions and choose life. And this is \"You uphold my lot\" — you uphold my hand to place it on the good lot and to choose it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:28.761961417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}